From 79016f86b837f6078c2b0ecef7b24c5176db1045 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Perrin <44126061+AlexPerrin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 04:48:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Treasure Trails: hard puzzle boxes

Hard anagram and cipher steps whose challenge is a puzzle box (cluehelper_challenge_box) now
hand out the step scroll's own box (<scroll>_puzzlebox), scrambled with 101 random slides from
the solved state (Mod Ash). Open shows the slide puzzle (306) with varp if1 = the box's picture
(castle 1, tree 2, troll 3; dbtable trail_puzzle_boxes from the OSRS Wiki's box ids) and the
pieces (enum 1864) in trail_puzzleinv; each client move (op1 on 306:4 with the slot) is
mirrored on the server. Talking to the npc with the solved box takes it and moves the trail on.
The npc lines are best guesses. Integration tests.
